  "kind": "necessary-localized-slice-definition-correction",
  "reason": "Actual CDR Theorem4.1 requires an R_n-homology ball, not a boundary homology isomorphism. For oriented B the single boundary fundamental class maps to zero, so the original condition is impossible; the literal original clause omitted orientation, and nonorientable examples can satisfy it when 2 is inverted (punctured RP4, boundary degree2). In particular standard B4 never satisfies the original boundary-inclusion criterion. The correction restores the source-defined homology-ball meaning, with all other claims retained.",
